{
 "about": "Parameters of the 2.5 strict checker (src/core/grammar), lifted from the ruling texts so that no grammar lives in code. Each entry names the ruling it comes from; a list a ruling leaves to the author (author_inputs_needed) is marked draft and its findings are reported as unruled, never as pass or fail. Edit here, never in code. 3.0 (proposed, ADR-0021): the vocative, apposition, absolute miyo, the liturgical formula, emphatic sela, commands, gagu after a work, acclamations and X krotiapo X, as rule parameters for the strict checker. 3.2 and 3.3 (proposed, ADR-0023): honorific titles, nationality adjectives and relational adjectives. 3.5 (proposed, ADR-0025): polygons and copied names of foreign things. 3.6 (proposed, ADR-0027): the copied names of drugs; the -san of a lexicalised diminutive (3.6:G153) is read by the 3.3:G148 rule.",
